      "content": "I understand your concern, and it's not just about being perfect, but also about maintaining a sense of control and accountability. I'd recommend implementing a \"pre-action review\" process, where you double-check and triple-check your work before submitting or completing a task. This could include creating a checklist or a workflow that includes a \"sanity check\" step to verify accuracy and attention to detail. Additionally, consider implementing a \"review and revise\" cycle, where you review your work, identify areas for improvement, and revise before finalizing. This will help you catch any errors or slips before they're noticed, and give you a sense of control over the auditing process.",
